      "risk_7d": "30% LOW",
      "next_update": null,
      "raw_text": "Off the East Coast of the United States:\nA strong non-tropical low pressure area is expected to form by \nSunday night off the southeast coast of the United States. This low \nis likely to move slowly and erratically through the middle of next \nweek, and some subtropical development is possible during this \ntime. Regardless of development, this system will cause high winds, \ncoastal flooding, and dangerous surf along portions of the U.S. East \nCoast. Please consult statements and warnings from local National \nWeather Service offices and the Weather Prediction Center for more \ninformation, along with High Seas Forecasts issued by the National \nWeather Service.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...near 0 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...30 percent.",
      "metadata": {
        "chance_48h_level": "LOW",
        "chance_48h_pct": "near 0",
        "chance_7d_level": "LOW",
        "chance_7d_pct": "30",
